Proceed to fault localisation and produce a step-by-step diagnosis.

"You probably mean org.apache.commons.compress.utils.IOUtils.skip(java.io.InputStream, long). It looks like:
```java
 94 :     public static long skip(InputStream input, long numToSkip) throws IOException {
 95 :         long available = numToSkip;
 96 :         while (numToSkip > 0) {
 97 :             long skipped = input.skip(numToSkip);
 98 :             if (skipped == 0) {
 99 :                 break;
100 :             }
101 :             numToSkip -= skipped;
102 :         }
103 :             
104 :         return available - numToSkip;
105 :     }
```"

The issue is with the `org.apache.commons.compress.utils.IOUtils.skip(InputStream, long)` method, not the test method as indicated in the bug report. The method implementation looks like this:

```java
94 :     public static long skip(InputStream input, long numToSkip) throws IOException {
95 :         long available = numToSkip;
96 :         while (numToSkip > 0) {
97 :             long skipped = input.skip(numToSkip);
98 :             if (skipped == 0) {
99 :                 break;
100 :             }
101 :             numToSkip -= skipped;
102 :         }
103 :             
104 :         return available - numToSkip;
105 :     }
```

The bug report mentions that `IOUtils.skip()` does not work as expected because it does not adhere to the contract it claims in the Javadoc. The Javadoc states that the method will only skip less than the requested number of bytes if the end of the input stream has been reached. 

The bug report also provides a snippet of code that seems to be the source of the issue:
```java
 long skipped = input.skip(numToSkip);  
 if (skipped == 0) 
{
    break;
}
```
This code snippet checks whether the number of bytes skipped is zero and breaks the loop if so. This behavior is not consistent with the Javadoc description.

Next, I will inspect the implementation of the `org.apache.commons.compress.utils.IOUtils.skip(InputStream, long)` method to further understand the root cause of the issue.

